    "narrative": "The lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP today leans heavily into efficiency against mid-tier arms, headlined by **Vinnie Pasquantino**, who boasts our highest score of 72.92. He is in a prime position hitting third against Montero, benefiting from a robust 11% boost due to the favorable SP matchup and a 14% platoon advantage. **Josh Naylor** (66.42) and **Seiya Suzuki** (60.05) also anchor the middle-to-bottom of our order as high-floor starts; **Seiya Suzuki** specifically gains traction against Rocker due to the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which provides a sneaky tailwind for our aggressive baserunning approach. **James Wood** (60.25) remains a must-start despite the tough matchup against Snelling; his placement in the leadoff spot and strong xwOBA profile keep his score firmly in the \"Strong\" territory.\n\nStrategic caution is required at the edges of the roster. **Corbin Carroll** (57.90) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (57.81) occupy the high-end of our \"Marginal\" tier, with **Tyler Soderstrom** receiving a significant 16% park-factor bump that helps him survive the challenge of facing Bradish. The most difficult decision of the day involved **Travis Bazzana**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a score of 39.99. While he offers intriguing speed, the combination of a difficult southpaw matchup against Prielipp and the \"Below Zebras\" floor rule necessitated a conservative approach to preserve our game caps. Meanwhile, investors should keep a close eye on **Brice Turang** and **Austin Riley**; both carry \"Lineup Pending\" designations, and should their actual batting orders drop significantly from our assumed placements, their marginal scores could dip further into sub-40 territory. Expect a grind against high-level arms like McLean, who poses a genuine hurdle for both **Gabriel Moreno** and **Corbin Carroll**.",
